{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/782834-invoking-the-dragon-s-ire","id":782834,"title":"Invoking the Dragon's Ire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T08:52:35-08:00","id":782834,"title":"Invoking the Dragon's Ire","content":"Rule clarification: The extra dice granted, are they used up, or are they used each turn of the coming scene? I'd been assuming the first, but if it's the second, I'll have to redo the changeling combat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:27:53-08:00","id":782861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/782834-invoking-the-dragon-s-ire#post782834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rule clarification: The extra dice granted, are they used up, or are they used each turn of the coming scene? I'd been assuming the first, but if it's the second, I'll have to redo the changeling combat...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be used each turn of the scene. Thats what I read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:29:12-08:00","id":782864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/782834-invoking-the-dragon-s-ire?p=782861#post782861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it should be used each turn of the scene. Thats what I read.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damnation! I shall have to redo all those combats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:31:12-08:00","id":782867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/782834-invoking-the-dragon-s-ire?p=782864#post782864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Damnation! I shall have to redo all those combats.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only do not add extra dice if you split your turn. If you split your turn to 3 part, it only give once but you can split that dice too. It won't give you 3 times in one turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T16:30:11-08:00","id":786335,"title":"","content":"The combat has been redone and the graphs reposted. With dragon's ire (3 dice) the Changeling is third, behind the demon and the dhampir, but beats the ghoul, the mummy, the hunter, and the human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:28:19-08:00","id":786789,"title":"","content":"Sounds more like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:07:06-08:00","id":787335,"title":"","content":"There's been some discussion as to whether Changelings soak aggravated damage or not. I would play them as being unable to do so; however, to be complete, I ran the battles with an aggravated-soaking changeling as well. So far, only the demon can inflict aggravated damage, so only the score against the demon changed (the other scores went up or down by 0-2%, which gives a good measure of the error in this process). Here is the plot (with the Dhampir included for comparison):<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23843264/Permanent/leth_vs_agg_Changeling.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Being able to soak aggravated made a big difference for the simple changeling, making it win - just! - against the demon (in actual fact, that should be exactly 50% - they have the same stats, and wield strength+2 weapons that the other can soak).<br /> <br /> But this effect was reduced at the strong level, with the win % going up only 5%.<br /> <br /> Where does this leave the rankings? Well, the (Strong) Demon was the only character type where the (Strong) Changeling performed better than the (Strong) Dhampir. With the ability to soak aggravated, they perform even better. But they still don't beat the Demon, and they still perform worse than the Dhampir against all other types. So the top of the podium is still Demon-Dhampir-Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:13:45-08:00","id":787344,"title":"","content":"Good stuff :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T09:08:13-08:00","id":787413,"title":"","content":"Which arts did you use? Could you please run this for Inanimae versus Demon also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T09:52:44-08:00","id":787457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/782834-invoking-the-dragon-s-ire?p=787413#post787413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which arts did you use?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The details can be found here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/778958-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-oh-the-humanity\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...h-the-humanity</a><br /> <br /> The Strong Changeling I stated as (note that because of a decision I made to ensure the characters were more comparable, the character has no free background points):<br /> <br /> Physical: 3/5/2<br /> Brawl/Melee/Athletics: 3/5/3<br /> Wits 5<br /> Willpower 5<br /> Remembrance 3<br /> <br /> The changeling was a Wilder Troll (+1 Strength, +1 wound). None-Sidhe can be allowed into Sidhe houses, if the GM allows if (Me-player: &quot;Can I?&quot; Me-GM: &quot;If you must...&quot;), so she was part of house Gwydion. Not for the positive benefit, but for the drawback - the ability to frenzy.<br /> <br /> The character dropped 5 points of chimera on a greatsword (damage Strength+6) and medium armour (+2). During her prep turn, she (split action) called upon the Wyrd and cast a cantrip using the second level of Wayfare, to get three extra actions (in the first turn only). She's stated so that she can expect to get three dice per turn from &quot;The Dragon's Ire.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 12-16-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T14:24:53-08:00","id":787628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/782834-invoking-the-dragon-s-ire?p=787457#post787457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The details can be found here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/778958-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-oh-the-humanity\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...h-the-humanity</a><br /> <br /> The Strong Changeling I stated as (note that because of a decision I made to ensure the characters were more comparable, the character has no free background points):<br /> <br /> Physical: 3/5/2<br /> Brawl/Melee/Athletics: 3/5/3<br /> Wits 5<br /> Willpower 5<br /> Remembrance 3<br /> <br /> The changeling was a Wilder Troll (+1 Strength, +1 wound). None-Sidhe can be allowed into Sidhe houses, if the GM allows if (Me-player: &quot;Can I?&quot; Me-GM: &quot;If you must...&quot;), so she was part of house Gwydion. Not for the positive benefit, but for the drawback - the ability to frenzy.<br /> <br /> The character dropped 5 points of chimera on a greatsword (damage Strength+6) and medium armour (+2). During her prep turn, she (split action) called upon the Wyrd and cast a cantrip using the second level of Wayfare, to get three extra actions (in the first turn only). She's stated so that she can expect to get three dice per turn from &quot;The Dragon's Ire.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I really want to see about Inanimae, since they are much more stronger than Kithian in terms of physical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}